STEP 1 → Add Maven Dependency

Apache POI dependency:

<dependency>
    <groupId>org.apache.poi</groupId>
    <artifactId>poi-ooxml</artifactId>
    <version>5.4.1</version>
</dependency>


STEP 2 → Provide the Excel File Path

Example:

String filepath1 = System.getProperty("user.dir")
        + "\\TestData\\TestData.xlsx";


STEP 3 → FileInputStream

FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream(filepath1);

→ FileInputStream loads/opens the Excel file as a stream
  so that Java can read its contents.


STEP 4 → Create Workbook → Sheet → Row → Cell

Workbook:
XSSFWorkbook workbook = new XSSFWorkbook(fis);

Sheet:
XSSFSheet sheet = workbook.getSheet("Sheet1");

Row:
sheet.getRow(rowIndex);

Cell:
sheet.getRow(rowIndex).getCell(columnIndex);

Interview memory trick:

getLastRowNum() → last index
getLastCellNum() → count

So getLastRowNum() → last index >>>>>>>>--Rows -- 5
getLastCellNum() → count ==>->>>>>>>>>>>>Columns -4